{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide","id":1528573,"title":"Looking at TC Players Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-14T16:07:36-08:00","id":1528573,"title":"Looking at TC Players Guide","content":"I have to say most of this is interesting, but there are bits that can be considered alienating approaches. (Like mentioning BLM ANTIFA by name in realtionship to a fictional organization, that can be taken as bad taste, in either a patronzing manner, or just pure contentious subject.) Now this was something akin to when Adventure had gone adnauseum about the evils of Facism, and then proceeded to give the most generous of passes to commununism, failing to mention the evils that the 20th century failed experiments in communism resulted in. <br /> I get it, the writers of this game are more on the left side of politics. But if going to Bible study has taught me anything, pushing your personal version of belief down some ones throat is going to result in rejection. The goal is to sell books, not fellate your self with a pat on the back cause of right thought. <br /> I love yalls books, but learn to use substitutes for RL groups, because while many groups had noble intentions or ideas, the execution, results, and flawed (arnt we all) people incharge of it, can lead to some rather pointed opinions on matters, best left out of silly fun games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T04:15:49-08:00","id":1528583,"title":"","content":"I disagree 100%, but I don\u2019t feel like arguing. Just wanted to get my opinion on the record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:55:11-08:00","id":1528681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide#post1528573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say most of this is interesting, but there are bits that can be considered alienating approaches. (Like mentioning BLM ANTIFA by name in realtionship to a fictional organization, that can be taken as bad taste, in either a patronzing manner, or just pure contentious subject.) Now this was something akin to when Adventure had gone adnauseum about the evils of Facism, and then proceeded to give the most generous of passes to commununism, failing to mention the evils that the 20th century failed experiments in communism resulted in.<br /> I get it, the writers of this game are more on the left side of politics. But if going to Bible study has taught me anything, pushing your personal version of belief down some ones throat is going to result in rejection. The goal is to sell books, not fellate your self with a pat on the back cause of right thought.<br /> I love yalls books, but learn to use substitutes for RL groups, because while many groups had noble intentions or ideas, the execution, results, and flawed (arnt we all) people incharge of it, can lead to some rather pointed opinions on matters, best left out of silly fun games.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you also filled up the book with the evils of capitalism to give the other side of the story, there wouldn't be any room left for the game, especially if you were using the same wide net typically used for attributing terrible things to communism. And as far as the time period for Adventure! went, people got jailed for being &quot;communists&quot; just for trying to start labor unions and get a fair shake from the bloated millionaires at the top of the heap, regardless of technical political ideology. And in the USA at present, we live with a lot of labor protections like minimum wage and health care exactly because the &quot;communists&quot; raised a fuss and ended up paying for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T08:01:06-08:00","id":1528714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1528681#post1528681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you also filled up the book with the evils of capitalism to give the other side of the story, there wouldn't be any room left for the game, especially if you were using the same wide net typically used for attributing terrible things to communism. And as far as the time period for Adventure! went, people got jailed for being &quot;communists&quot; just for trying to start labor unions and get a fair shake from the bloated millionaires at the top of the heap, regardless of technical political ideology. And in the USA at present, we live with a lot of labor protections like minimum wage and health care exactly because the &quot;communists&quot; raised a fuss and ended up paying for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look I get it, I am all for Universal Health Care, Unions, equal rights, against corporatism and the general dickery that goes on behind the doors of power. What I am talking about is using real-world political movements and organizations and tying them and their ability to function to fictional secret super societies (ones whose background material would charitably described as not adverse to using terrorism to achieve its objectives). That is in a word, &quot;Tacky&quot;, which is why I think that somewhat obvious substitutes be used instead, or not at all.<br /> <br /> I am also not comparing the social programs of the rest of Europe and the 20th Century Labor movement to COMMUNISM. I know Communism was a dirty word used to scare little old church ladies to action, and was tied to anyone who disagreed with Neo-Liberal economic/political policy. I am talking about the authoritarian nightmare known as Stalinism and Maoism, and all the worst versions that seem to pop up in these countries that take the shortcut (revolutions, purges, and blind redistribution) to build some pie-in-the-sky dream of a socialist utopia, but really existed to feed into the ego of tyrant. Also, the Communism we are most familiar with is the USSR and PRC. You know, the nightmare kind, the kind that people I know grew up with and experienced firsthand. Hell one of my favorite philosophers a self-avowed communist, says that the 20th century experiments with it turned into a most horrible mistake, a mistake that is still affecting their people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T11:35:41-08:00","id":1528725,"title":"","content":"I agree about mentioning real world organizations, specially those that may have good intentions and has proven to be lead by not so well intended people. Violence is never a way, period.<br /> <br /> Now on the communism X capitalism part, it\u2019s fun that people point to Russia, Cuba and China and say: \u201cSee, people are hungry there, and that\u2019s because of communism.\u201d<br /> <br /> It they don\u2019t see those\u2019d countries without the communism, it\u2019s always comparing them to the Western Europe and USA, but Africa and Latin America are mostly capitalists, yet we have a lot of hungry people here.<br /> <br /> Russia was the poorest country in Europe until the communist revolution, and in 20 years it was a world power.<br /> China was so poor people were dying there before the revolution.<br /> Cuba was no better than a Haiti before the revolution.<br /> Those Countries were shit places, as are all the 3rd world countries, communism actually gave them some relevance.<br /> South America governments killed thousands of our own people in the name of capitalism, dictatorships funded by USA to prevent dictatorships funded by USSR, and people was still dying of famine the last time I looked out of my window. <br /> <br /> The entire problem is not the Captalism X Communism, it\u2019s all about when controls the money. So\u2026 yes, communism is bad, capitalism is bad, people are horrible and this kind of discussion takes us nowhere, specially since the fall of USSR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T15:02:08-08:00","id":1528755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1528714#post1528714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look I get it, I am all for Universal Health Care, Unions, equal rights, against corporatism and the general dickery that goes on behind the doors of power. What I am talking about is using real-world political movements and organizations and tying them and their ability to function to fictional secret super societies (ones whose background material would charitably described as not adverse to using terrorism to achieve its objectives). That is in a word, &quot;Tacky&quot;, which is why I think that somewhat obvious substitutes be used instead, or not at all.<br /> <br /> I am also not comparing the social programs of the rest of Europe and the 20th Century Labor movement to COMMUNISM. I know Communism was a dirty word used to scare little old church ladies to action, and was tied to anyone who disagreed with Neo-Liberal economic/political policy. I am talking about the authoritarian nightmare known as Stalinism and Maoism, and all the worst versions that seem to pop up in these countries that take the shortcut (revolutions, purges, and blind redistribution) to build some pie-in-the-sky dream of a socialist utopia, but really existed to feed into the ego of tyrant. Also, the Communism we are most familiar with is the USSR and PRC. You know, the nightmare kind, the kind that people I know grew up with and experienced firsthand. Hell one of my favorite philosophers a self-avowed communist, says that the 20th century experiments with it turned into a most horrible mistake, a mistake that is still affecting their people.</div> </div> </div> </div>All my homies hate Lysenko, Stalin and Mao.<br /> <br /> That said, communism in the 20th century doesn't make for a good experiment; not with spy agencies with their thumbs on the scales, or the Cold War making for exploitable situations everywhere. The only things we've really learned is that people who have lots of money really hate communism and will go to any length to try and unseat it, and that Russia and China have a really difficult time not being in control. Because the purges in the USSR are really more of a holdover from what people learned in Tsarist times, when the gulag system was created. And if you had been independent and didn't want to be in Russia anymore, you could expect to be doing hard labor in the Russian Far East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T11:17:21-07:00","id":1538531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1528755#post1528755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All my homies hate Lysenko, Stalin and Mao.<br /> <br /> That said, communism in the 20th century doesn't make for a good experiment; not with spy agencies with their thumbs on the scales, or the Cold War making for exploitable situations everywhere. The only things we've really learned is that people who have lots of money really hate communism and will go to any length to try and unseat it, and that Russia and China have a really difficult time not being in control. Because the purges in the USSR are really more of a holdover from what people learned in Tsarist times, when the gulag system was created. And if you had been independent and didn't want to be in Russia anymore, you could expect to be doing hard labor in the Russian Far East.</div> </div> </div> </div>USSR had better spies in the KGB as the CIA was remit to admit it, but they did admit that USSR was better at it than the USA, the west was just able to react better and faster at the macro scale with its distributed leadership systems (ie the left hand rarely had an idea what the right was up to, nevermind what the feet or ears were doing), the problem is that communism is a flawed utopian ideal, most philosophies only work in a frame work of fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a system cant survive outside influence then it is a bad system, and those systems fail because of human nature. the nature of revolutions not really being conducive for establishing a sturdy government, and easily open for influence for strongmen and charismatic leaders with an authoritarian bent. At the end of the day, what matters is that the people have a sense of security (food, housing, employment, toilet flushes, train on time and future), how it accomplishes that it is a non factor as long as it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T13:25:24-07:00","id":1538534,"title":"","content":"Six months? You might be arguing with a subtly different person in that time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1538531#post1538531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> USSR had better spies in the KGB as the CIA was remit to admit it, but they did admit that USSR was better at it than the USA, the west was just able to react better and faster at the macro scale with its distributed leadership systems (ie the left hand rarely had an idea what the right was up to, nevermind what the feet or ears were doing), the problem is that communism is a flawed utopian ideal, most philosophies only work in a frame work of fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a system cant survive outside influence then it is a bad system, and those systems fail because of human nature. the nature of revolutions not really being conducive for establishing a sturdy government, and easily open for influence for strongmen and charismatic leaders with an authoritarian bent. At the end of the day, what matters is that the people have a sense of security (food, housing, employment, toilet flushes, train on time and future), how it accomplishes that it is a non factor as long as it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget outside influence; tying yourself internally to big business seems like it's going to be the end of us as an entirely self-destructive matter. Shareholders having the biggest say in anyone's well-being in a system made solely for profit extraction doesn't have a good prognosis, and here the Project 2025 people aiming to get into office want that to be the only kind of system available. Socialist leanings are the only things holding up a lot of what could be considered even remotely fair capitalism, and it's still too much for people with far too much money for anyone's good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T11:02:28-07:00","id":1538570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1538534#post1538534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six months? You might be arguing with a subtly different person in that time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Forget outside influence; tying yourself internally to big business seems like it's going to be the end of us as an entirely self-destructive matter. Shareholders having the biggest say in anyone's well-being in a system made solely for profit extraction doesn't have a good prognosis, and here the Project 2025 people aiming to get into office want that to be the only kind of system available. Socialist leanings are the only things holding up a lot of what could be considered even remotely fair capitalism, and it's still too much for people with far too much money for anyone's good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been busy, <br /> the thing is, i am for socialised programgs and support, and a regulated economy. <br /> the problem is that communism has this great idea of a free society, and tackling its woes, but fails at one cruceal component. How to stop a ruling class from taking over with out having yet another violent revolution. The way communist nations did it resulted in a corrupt class, and created a worse scenario than the slow route through socialized programs. <br /> we saw this in the various communsit revolutions and the French revolution. How the US managed to avoid eating it self was the annomoly.<br /> <br /> But my original point still stands, Adventure is quick to point to Facism and Capitalism but not be equally critical of Communism. <br /> too many communists are always falling for the the No True Scottman Falacy. Instead realising that as a system its just too vulnerable to human greed to ever work, Corporatetism though, that monstrous entity works as intended, and creates the nightmare we are looking at. <br /> it's why I look more at the how, than just the what groups want to accomplish, that is where the terror hides.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T12:44:59-07:00","id":1538582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1528573-looking-at-tc-players-guide?p=1538570#post1538570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been busy,<br /> the thing is, i am for socialised programgs and support, and a regulated economy.<br /> the problem is that communism has this great idea of a free society, and tackling its woes, but fails at one cruceal component. How to stop a ruling class from taking over with out having yet another violent revolution. The way communist nations did it resulted in a corrupt class, and created a worse scenario than the slow route through socialized programs.<br /> we saw this in the various communsit revolutions and the French revolution. How the US managed to avoid eating it self was the annomoly.<br /> <br /> But my original point still stands, Adventure is quick to point to Facism and Capitalism but not be equally critical of Communism.<br /> too many communists are always falling for the the No True Scottman Falacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So who's a true capitalist? Just the people following social convention, or are we also including the ones that race to the top and kick the ladder out so that they run everything forever? The ones who are making it so that capitalism turns into a self-devouring serpent?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead realising that as a system its just too vulnerable to human greed to ever work, Corporatetism though, that monstrous entity works as intended, and creates the nightmare we are looking at.<br /> it's why I look more at the how, than just the what groups want to accomplish, that is where the terror hides.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be that, with so many writers coming from the USA, they might feel that there was plenty of anti-communist sentiment around them already. You can't help but fucking choke on it after decades of Cold War. In that atmosphere, it might not seem particularly important to have to &quot;warn&quot; people about it because they already know a dozen people who ramble on about conspiracy theories about how the schools are all run by communists and there's a plot to make all the kids commies and more lines that you'd expect from General Ripper.<br /> <br /> (I was in school in the time frame that they were talking about, I can tell you that anyone espousing communism in any US school is definitely an outlier.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}